From 77057f5b47de6acadce81c075d466ed30698b756 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:21:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: validate contiguous DMA plane coverage

The LTS probe already sets the mapper segment limit. Replace its
overly strict single-segment guard with validation that adjacent
mapped segments cover the image plane. Reject gaps and insufficient
coverage, and leave unused tails unrestricted. Actual ARM mapper and
buffer callbacks pass 46 synthetic checks; the previous guard fails
five. Three targeted regressions fail six, eight and three checks
respectively.

The complete camera set builds 78 native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT
objects without W=1 diagnostics or permissive CFI. Source checksums
match ELF line tables. Three source-only CAMSS partial links retain no
unresolved MIPI timing helper; these are not final Kbuild module or
kernel links. Low-level hardware, locks, full PM/driver core and
capture are modeled or untested. Physical acceptance and the r2
display fault remain open.

Original proposals are by Timothy Schmidt with Claude Opus 5.5
assistance; Codex (GPT-6) prepared this maintained-LTS reconciliation
and qualification. Original author/date and all source/license notices
are preserved. Human DCO and review remain pending; no sign-off, phone
action or publication is claimed.

Backported from commit fdadb178ffed ("media: qcom: camss: Carry
qualified ARM32 linear DMA ranges")
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c   | 23 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
index 1429a05ca22b0..59b21b3a723d1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
@@ -152,18 +152,31 @@ static int video_buf_init(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 	const struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane *format =
 						&video->active_fmt.fmt.pix_mp;
 	struct sg_table *sgt;
-	unsigned int i;
+	struct scatterlist *s;
+	dma_addr_t expected;
+	unsigned long size;
+	unsigned int i, j;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < format->num_planes; i++) {
 		sgt = vb2_dma_sg_plane_desc(vb, i);
 		if (!sgt)
 			return -EFAULT;
 
-		/* The hardware writes each plane linearly from its base. */
-		if (sgt->nents != 1) {
+		/* Adjacent DMA segments may cover one linear image plane. */
+		expected = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl);
+		size = 0;
+		for_each_sgtable_dma_sg(sgt, s, j) {
+			if (sg_dma_address(s) != expected)
+				break;
+			size += sg_dma_len(s);
+			if (size >= format->plane_fmt[i].sizeimage)
+				break;
+			expected += sg_dma_len(s);
+		}
+		if (size < format->plane_fmt[i].sizeimage) {
 			dev_err_ratelimited(video->camss->dev,
-					    "Buffer plane %u spans %u DMA segments\n",
-					    i, sgt->nents);
+					    "Buffer plane %u is not contiguous\n",
+					    i);
 			return -EFAULT;
 		}
 
